# All 6,656 `is_boolean` assertions as one edge list

The edge-list unit in practice. `allBoolEdges` matches every instance against `tnBool` in
13 slices of 512 (~7 s each, 13.7 ms/edge) composed by `edgesMatch_of_chunks`. One decide over
all 6,656 at once also works but needs close to the 16 GB cap and is not reliably reproducible; `allBoolBits` then
concludes booleanity for every bit in the circuit from that one check plus `tmpl_isBool`.

There is no per-assertion module, no per-assertion lemma, and no per-assertion algebra. The
baseline was a per-node `have`-chain at 104 ms/node, i.e. ~2,077 s for these same 6,656
three-node cones -- and, more to the point, 6,656 separate proofs.

`assertOfB` and `bitOfB` are bisections over the edge index, the same shape `nodeFn` and
`wireFn` use; `mapOfB e i` is the instance map `coneIs` now takes as a function.
-/

